 *> Armor trims (54 section 18.4): the palettes, the pattern names and the recolouring of a trim pattern texture.
 *> Palette numbers: 1 to 11 the trim materials in registry order (amethyst, copper, diamond, emerald, gold, iron, lapis, netherite, quartz, redstone, resin: the
 *> material holder of a trim is its position + 1, so the holder is the palette number), 12 to 16 the darker variants (iron, copper, gold, diamond, netherite).
 *> Pattern numbers 1 to 18 in registry order (bolt ... wild: the holder of a trim pattern is the number).

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TRIM-PALETTE-FOR.
*> USING armor asset (1 leather, 2 copper, 3 chainmail, 4 iron, 5 gold, 6 diamond, 7 turtle scute, 8 netherite: ENTITY-ARMOR-ASSET), material holder 1 to 11, palette out:
*> the material's palette, or its `_darker` variant when the trim material is the armor's own material (iron, copper, gold, diamond, netherite: 54 section 18.4 rule 2).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-ASSET                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-MATERIAL             BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-PALETTE              BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-ASSET L-MATERIAL L-PALETTE.
     MOVE L-MATERIAL TO L-PALETTE
     EVALUATE TRUE
         WHEN L-ASSET = 4 AND L-MATERIAL = 6
             MOVE 12 TO L-PALETTE
         WHEN L-ASSET = 2 AND L-MATERIAL = 2
             MOVE 13 TO L-PALETTE
         WHEN L-ASSET = 5 AND L-MATERIAL = 5
             MOVE 14 TO L-PALETTE
         WHEN L-ASSET = 6 AND L-MATERIAL = 3
             MOVE 15 TO L-PALETTE
         WHEN L-ASSET = 8 AND L-MATERIAL = 8
             MOVE 16 TO L-PALETTE
         WHEN OTHER
             CONTINUE
     END-EVALUATE
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TRIM-PALETTE-FOR.

